# One-way notes between the native plugin and modules/vrcam_select.lua. The folder has to exist
# because Lua only writes here (io.open "w" will not create a directory) -- hence this file.
#
#   vrcam_enable.txt   native -> Lua. "1" or "0": the overlay's Enable/Disable VRCAM button.
#   vrcam_active.txt   Lua -> native. The virtualCameraName of the component actually enabled,
#                      read back off the live component so the view key comes from the asset
#                      rather than from a naming assumption.
#
# Both are rewritten in place and polled; neither is a queue. Nothing else lives here any more --
# the old command.json / status.json pair belonged to the testbed dxgi.dll and is gone with it.
